1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,400
The queen is the most powerful piece

2
00:00:02,211 --> 00:00:02,939
in chess.

3
00:00:03,067 --> 00:00:04,918
But for centuries it was the weakest

4
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:05,469
on the board.

5
00:00:05,902 --> 00:00:07,799
In medieval chess it could move just

6
00:00:07,611 --> 00:00:09,061
one square diagonally.

7
00:00:09,189 --> 00:00:11,063
It was a counsellor, not a queen.

8
00:00:11,482 --> 00:00:14,193
In the late fifteenth century everything changes:

9
00:00:14,395 --> 00:00:16,086
the queen and the bishop gain the

10
00:00:15,897 --> 00:00:17,382
long moves they have today.

11
00:00:17,806 --> 00:00:19,589
The first printed book on that new

12
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,985
game is written by Lucena, a student

13
00:00:21,797 --> 00:00:25,173
at Salamanca, in 1497 at the latest.

14
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:26,867
He calls it the queen's chess.

15
00:00:27,298 --> 00:00:28,851
In Italy it got another name:

16
00:00:29,018 --> 00:00:30,101
alla rabiosa.

17
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:31,542
The furious way.

18
00:00:31,966 --> 00:00:33,141
Did Spain invent it?

19
00:00:33,269 --> 00:00:35,327
Nobody knows who first moved the queen

20
00:00:35,138 --> 00:00:35,763
that way.

21
00:00:35,895 --> 00:00:37,299
What we do know is where it

22
00:00:37,111 --> 00:00:38,240
was first printed.

23
00:00:38,674 --> 00:00:40,411
Share it with the person who always

24
00:00:40,222 --> 00:00:41,236
beats you at chess.

